<Base title="Groove Dice Pack Builder — macOS & Windows | Kim’s Work" description={p.summary}>
<article class="wrap guide"><a class="back" href={url('software/apps/')}>← Apps</a><p class="eyebrow">DESKTOP APP / VERSION {p.version}</p><h1>Your folders.<br/>Your next sound pack.</h1><p class="lead">{p.summary}</p><p>Choose a source folder, review instrument mapping, generate and audition kits, then export an independent .gdexp. Your source files stay where they are. No Python installation is needed for the packaged app.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href={p.mac}>Download for macOS · Apple Silicon ↓</a><a class="button" href={p.windows}>Download for Windows · x64 ↓</a></div><p><a href={url('apps/groove-dice-pack-builder/manual/')}>Read the complete manual →</a> · <a href={p.release}>Release notes & checksums ↗</a></p><figure class="detail-image"><img src={url(`images/${p.image}`)} alt="Actual Pack Builder app showing original sound folders, eight instrument cards and generated kits" width="1450" height="968"/><figcaption>Actual macOS application. Pack ID is automatically generated and kept under Advanced pack settings.</figcaption></figure>
<section><h2>From source folder to playable pack.</h2><ol><li>Map Kick, Snare, Closed/Open Hat, Clap, Tom, Cymbal and Perc folders.</li><li>Generate kits, choose individual sounds, set levels and lock parts before another roll.</li><li>Audition a two-bar beat at your BPM and swing, then export a .gdexp.</li><li>Install the pack into Groove Dice Content and reopen the instrument.</li></ol></section>
<section><h2>A project you can return to.</h2><p>Save your source mapping, kit choices, locks, metadata and rights in a .gdproject. Keep it with its source folder when moving between computers. The stable pack identifier lets saved songs reconnect after an update; it is not a user account.</p></section>
<section><h2>Compatibility & validation</h2><ul><li>macOS Apple Silicon and Windows x64 packages. Windows backend, GUI and bundled-app smoke tests run on Windows CI; Mac tests run on Apple Silicon.</li><li>PCM WAV and standard PPQ MIDI. Float/compressed WAV requires conversion. Auto MIDI mapping handles native Groove Dice notes and General MIDI drums.</li><li>Missing instruments require an explicit choice to use generated silence. No files are borrowed from other installed packs.</li><li>macOS is ad-hoc signed and not notarized; Windows binaries are not code-signed. Your OS may show an unknown-publisher notice. Inspect the release and checksum before opening.</li><li>Real Windows audio-device coverage and every hardware combination are not certified.</li></ul><p>This app uses <a href="https://ffmpeg.org/">FFmpeg</a> under LGPL 2.1+ through Qt Multimedia. <a href="https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-7.1.2.tar.xz">Corresponding FFmpeg source</a> and the bundled notices document those dependencies. <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/mpc-software/apps/public/GrooveDicePackBuilder/THIRD_PARTY.md`}>All software notices and source links ↗</a></p></section>
<section><h2>Try a real result.</h2><p><a href={url('expansions/groove-dice/workshop-sessions/')}>Workshop Sessions</a> was exported through the actual desktop app and tested with Groove Dice. Its original sounds are included in a separate expansion file.</p></section>
</article></Base>
